{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"46","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Ball Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A kindergarten teacher Natalia Pavlovna has invented a new ball game. This game not only develops the children's physique, but also teaches them how to count. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The game goes as follows. Kids stand in circle. Let's agree to think of the children as numbered with numbers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" clockwise and the child number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is holding the ball. First the first child throws the ball to the next one clockwise, i.e. to the child number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the child number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" throws the ball to the next but one child, i.e. to the child number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the fourth child throws the ball to the child that stands two children away from him, i.e. to the child number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the ball is thrown to the child who stands "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" children away from the child number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the ball is thrown to the child who stands "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" children away from the last one, and so on. It should be mentioned that when a ball is thrown it may pass the beginning of the circle. For example, if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n = 5"},{"kind":"text","text":", then after the third throw the child number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" has the ball again. Overall, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" throws are made, and the game ends."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem is that not all the children get the ball during the game. If a child doesn't get the ball, he gets very upset and cries until Natalia Pavlovna gives him a candy. That's why Natalia Pavlovna asks you to help her to identify the numbers of the children who will get the ball after each throw."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":") which indicates the number of kids in the circle."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the single line print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers which are the numbers of children who will get the ball after each throw. Separate the numbers by spaces."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 4 7 1 6 2 9 7 6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"46A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/46/problem/A"}